{
  "id": "ep162",
  "duration": 46.492,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.915,
      "text": "Space Shuttle Atlantis lost over seven hundred thermal tiles during flight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlantis taking off on STS-27.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantis_taking_off_on_STS-27.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.267,
          "end": 4.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.915,
      "end": 12.96,
      "text": "On December 2, 1988, ablative insulating material from the right solid rocket booster struck the orbiter.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.9,
          "end": 12.967,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.96,
      "end": 18.555,
      "text": "Eighty-five seconds into ascent, severe debris tore into the ship's vulnerable belly.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Thermal protection system inspections from ISS - Shuttle bottom.jpg",
        "credit": "Nasa",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thermal_protection_system_inspections_from_ISS_-_Shuttle_bottom.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.967,
          "end": 15.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.767,
          "end": 18.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.555,
      "end": 25.25,
      "text": "Using the Canadarm, the crew inspected the heavy damage and grainy images were sent to Mission Control.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Wake Shield Facility on STS-60 (STS060-74-054).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wake_Shield_Facility_on_STS-60_(STS060-74-054).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.567,
          "end": 21.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 21.933,
          "end": 25.267,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.25,
      "end": 32.645,
      "text": "Engineers dismissed the footage as mere lights and shadows, leaving commander Robert Hoot Gibson convinced they would die.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS-27 crew poses for inflight portrait on forward flight deck with football.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS-27_crew_poses_for_inflight_portrait_on_forward_flight_deck_with_football.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.267,
          "end": 27.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.867,
          "end": 32.633,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.645,
      "end": 40.195,
      "text": "Atlantis survived fiery reentry because a missing tile sat squarely over a thick aluminum antenna plate.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Sts-27 Landing.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sts-27_Landing.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 32.633,
          "end": 36.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 36.4,
          "end": 40.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.195,
      "end": 46.142,
      "text": "Over seven hundred thermal tiles were missing when Space Shuttle Atlantis finally returned to Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlantis taking off on STS-27.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantis_taking_off_on_STS-27.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.2,
